# The step 25 fixes, part `secrets`: the review's findings 2, 3 and 4, and
# the review of those fixes. A token the first run draws [redacted] is
# [redacted] in every view that displays the configuration, and the trust
# question shows a project's shared file whole; credential names the import
# did not know; a header's variable its own and none of the harness's
# (docs/steps/step-25-fixes/parts/secrets.md).

[break] the-views-show-an-imported-token
rule: Every view of the configuration shows an MCP server's command line by the import's rule.
file: crates/cineris-config/src/schema/redact.rs
in: redact_reserved
find: command_line(key.last(), value)
replace: command_line(None, value)
caught-by:
    cineris-config::it imports::what_the_first_run_hid_is_hidden_by_every_view
    cineris-config::it imports::a_hand_written_server_is_shown_by_the_same_rule

[break] config-get-shows-an-imported-token
rule: config/get, and so /config, shows an MCP server's arguments as the first run did.
file: crates/cineris-config/src/schema/redact.rs
in: command_line
find: ("args", Value::Array(items)) =>
replace: ("arguments", Value::Array(items)) =>
packages: cineris-core
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it reload::config_get_shows_an_imported_token_as_the_first_run_did

[break] the-guess-passes-over-a-list
rule: In a reserved section a table inside a list has its keys looked at.
file: crates/cineris-config/src/schema/redact.rs
